         "Yes, and more than one option. ePegboard is free for clubs. SportRevive is free. ShuttlePilot is free while in beta. ShuttlSync is free up to two live courts and ShuttleStats charges a fee per member payment rather than a subscription. Check the current pricing page before rollout, because these change."),
        ("Do players have to create accounts?",
         "Not with ePegboard. A club night runs entirely from a shared screen with no player sign-ups at all, which matters because compulsory onboarding is where a rollout usually stalls. Accounts only start to earn their place if you want players to see their own history and ratings between sessions, and that stays optional."),
        ("Should club-night software work offline?",
         "Only if you cannot rely on a connection at the venue, counting mobile data or a hotspot as well as the hall's own Wi-Fi. Where you genuinely cannot, it matters a lot. Court Manager documents offline operation in unusual detail, including handling venue login pages that interfere with it, and ShuttlSync supports offline sessions. ePegboard's web app needs a connection; its Windows desktop version runs fully offline but is a separate paid product that is no longer being developed, so we would not recommend choosing us on that basis. Test the actual failure mode before committing, not just whether the word offline appears on a page."),
        ("How do I run a fair club night without software at all?",
